From 2794710eb6185336b2ad6eaf2d1d8174de41f4f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:02:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 021/181] Input: Add a driver for Hynitron CST66xx SPI
 touchscreens

The CST66xx series take big-endian commands in their own SPI message
and answer in the next message, clocked by a zero-filled transmit
buffer. After reset the firmware takes 50 ms to start. A 2-byte wake-up
and three work-mode commands follow, then 0xD0030000 returns the panel
information (chip type, firmware, resolution, channel counts). On each
falling edge of the interrupt, 0xD0070000 returns the touch report: 9
bytes, 5 more per further contact, guarded by a 16-bit sum, then
acknowledged with 0xD00002AB.

The protocol follows Hynitron's GPLv2 driver for the family; there is
no public datasheet.
